1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,680
Meet kinhin.

2
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:04,820
The mindful CI.

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:09,650
A self-hosted runner does one job at a time.

4
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:15,570
Your queue waits its turn, and whatever one
job leaves behind, the next one inherits.

5
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:19,920
kinhin is a free, open-source Mac app.

6
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:26,120
It starts a fresh VM or container for each job,
and deletes it when the job is done.

7
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:32,100
Jobs arrive, and kinhin scales to
the queue, within your Mac's limits.

8
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:35,070
Each job gets its own clean instance.

9
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:40,250
macOS VMs and Linux
containers run side by side.

10
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,720
When one fails, the next still
starts on a clean machine.

11
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:49,020
Then every instance is
deleted. Nothing lingers.

12
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:52,300
Install with one line.

13
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,420
Then kinhin doctor checks your Mac.

14
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:07,750
It works with GitHub, GitLab, Gitea and Forgejo,
on Tart, apple container, or Docker.

15
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:12,480
One job. One VM. Gone when it's done.

16
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:17,350
kinhin.dev. Free, Apache 2.0,
no telemetry, in beta.
